<title>USA: Japan, Russia agree on new investment program.</title>
<headline>Japan, Russia agree on new investment program.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan will expand its investment into Russia under an agreement reached on Friday, a Japanese spokesman told reporters.</p>
<p>The pact was made during a meeting between President Boris Yeltsin and Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto ahead of the G7 summit here, which Russia is also attending.</p>
<p>They agreed to set up a governmental-level committee to study cooperation, a Japanese statement said.</p>
<p>Possible areas include promotion of investment in financial systems aimed at effective use of savings in Russia, it said.</p>
</text>
